      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a start, but it feels a bit vague or even a little confusing with the \"May-Comes\" thing. and honestly, in 1954 Alabama, the tension wouldn't just be about immigrants, it would be much more intense regarding the local Black community and the civil rights movements starting to pick up steam. to make it feel real and gritty for a prestige drama, can you rewrite it? i need the dialogue to be more blunt about their views on segregation and how they feel about the town changing. make it feel like they're actually expressing the prejudices of the time without holding back too much for the sake of the \"prestige\" feel.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
